# Rules: versioned prompt library

## PROJECT FACTS (edit these)
- Layout: prompts/<name>/v<N>.md (+ optional meta.yaml)
- Loader: src/prompts.(ts|py) loads prompts by name + version
- Test: `npm test` | `pytest -q`
- Prompt regression check: `make prompt-check`

## Must pass before done
- Tests pass. `make prompt-check` passes (or report the cases that changed).

## Versioning
- Never edit a released prompt version in place. Copy it to v<N+1> and change the copy.
- Every prompt version has meta: owner, intended model, variables, date, and a one-line changelog entry.
- Code pins a prompt version explicitly. No 'latest' in production paths.

## Prompt content
- Declare every template variable in meta. Rendering fails on a missing or unused variable.
- Keep instructions, context and examples in clearly separated sections.
- Put the output format last, with an exact schema or example.
- No secrets, customer data or internal URLs inside prompt files.
- Treat user-provided text as data: wrap it in delimiters and never let it replace the instructions.

## Changes
- One prompt change per commit, with before/after outputs on the regression cases.
- Do not change a prompt and the model it targets in the same commit.

## Boundaries
- Do not delete old versions that code still references. Search before removing.

## Definition of done
- New version + meta + changelog line + regression results attached to the PR.
